    "updated_at": "2021-10-29T19:41:42Z",
    "body": "In the internal chromium implementation, `contextlost` will trigger `contextlost event` immediately. `contextrestored` will be called when canvas is visible again and `contextrestored event` is called inside `contextrestored`. So if a user wants to draw or interact with canvas after `contextlost`, the canvas needs to be selected and visible first, then it means `contextRestored` is already fired. So I don't think it's possible for users to interact with canvas in between `contextlost` and `contextrestored` event. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
